osed on a planted `return false`. The one-arm problem is resolved by mutation rather than message: 93 of 112 mutants kill exactly one subtest and every overlap is one of the two documented structural shapes.\n- **G-C/G-D.** Both `EncodeRequest` entries driven independently, 4/4. No resurrections and none structurally possible — production byte-identical to rev2 across all eight files, test inventory 92→98 with **zero removals**. Coverage 83.3→87.6 accounted per function: 11 `query.go` validators to 100%, exactly the C1/C2 surface.\n\n### Non-blocking (recorded, not gating)\n`internal/dirnode` isn't imported by any command yet — same as the accepted `sessadapter`/`provhost` leaves, a Story integration step. The deadline row keys its out-of-range branch on hardcoded `0`/`3600001`, so moving the row's min/max without them would quietly degrade it — stated in the comment, three lines apart. And `round3.md` has a stray non-English token in prose.\n\nEvidence attached: `TASK-260830-ljkj8r_review-verdict-rev3.md`, `TASK-260830-ljkj8r_review-mutant-log-rev3.tsv`. Integration needs a new tracked run bound to `developer`/`implementer` — not mine to close.","ttft_ms":1915,"type":"result","duration_ms":1615679,"uuid":"2db39997-9b12-44a0-9c5b-2e7bd9a43ec8","ttft_stream_ms":1079,"time_to_request_ms":21,"first_content_frame_ms":1079,"queued_turn_count":0}
